The combination of all event-level cuts yielded a sample of 12\(\times\)10\({}^{6}\) minimum bias, full-field events.

### 3.3 Electron Identification

J/\(\psi\) mesons have a 5.88% chance of decaying via the dimuon channel, 5.93% via the dielectron channel, and the rest of the time via decays that involve hadronic

Figure 3.2: The minimum bias primary track charged multiplicity distribution, \(N_{ch}\), in the pseudorapidity region of \(|\eta|\)\(<\) 0.5. The three centrality classes used in this analysis are shown.

